WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
## SIGNS ##

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:22.000
There are times when you go to bed only to realize that maybe
you should have wiped better, so you have a hard time going to sleep

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.650
Hello, everyone.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.500
I'm Sakata Gintoki.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.880
I'm Shimura Shinpachi.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.880
I'm Kagura.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.090
It's nice to see you again.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.950
Hey, should we really start up like this?

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.210
Won't people be weirded out without that static exterior shot?

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.950
I-It's fine!

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.940
After a year of not seeing someone, a simple introduction can't hurt.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.530
Gin! It's been too long, I'm feeling really nervous!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.180
It's like a classroom on the first
day after summer vacation!

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.960
I'm not even sure how to modulate
my voice or my volume!

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.510
Actually, is this how my voice is supposed to sound?

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:07.680
Is this how I talk-gin?

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.000
You don't have vocal tics like that, no.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.260
Y'know, I get the feeling my voice is weird too.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.340
It's like I should sound more moe or something?

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.930
So don't get the wrong idea, okay?!

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.570
You're the one with the wrong idea!

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.910
It's too late to try and change your personalities now!

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.170
Come on you two, get it together!

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.190
It's been a long time, so let's start with a greeting!

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.400
Uh, when people talk about a "limited renewal," they can mean a lot of things...

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:39.810
I just realized something...

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.870
Isn't this like the intro they do with Drift Daibakusho?

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.780
It's like when Cho makes small talk before the comedy sketches start, right?

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.100
Isn't that a little cliche?

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.600
We should've done the Kaminari sketch instead!

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.370
We could pull it off if Shinpachi plays guitar and sings like Nakamoto!

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.350
They kind of have the same kind
of position in the cast, too.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.610
That sort of "air-like" presence.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.530
Air has no presence, dammit!

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.030
Kouji was always great in the callisthenics corner, too!

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.470
Can we just do this, already?!

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.480
We've got a special one-shot episode for you all today.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.020
It's not really that cool, though!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.070
We were gonna do this in the first episode of the second series

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.090
but since we started with the "Two Years Later" story arc we couldn't find a spot to put it!

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:23.480
The fact that we're showing it now after the show's done and over is ironic.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.160
Hey! Don't just blurt stuff like that out in passing!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.010
I'm sure some of you know what we're talking about because of that last conversation,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.240
but we hope you enjoy it anyway.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:43.430
The input for this super move is too hard and I can't pull it off

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.670
Awaken...

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.590
You, the chosen ones!

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:58.180
This time, you will actually unleash
your hidden inner power!

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:06.950
Open your eyes, and the door to your new potential!

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.820
Awaken!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.490
Where are we?

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.920
Good morning...

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.500
What is this? Where are we?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.810
How the hell am I supposed to know?

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.430
I just woke up here myself.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.160
Is there a blackout?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.780
It'd be weird how clearly we can see each other, if that was the case.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.690
Actually, didn't something like this happen before?

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:36.150
Damn it all... My head hurts from a hangover...

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.000
Sorry, but I'm going back to sleep—

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.070
You shall not!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.990
This time, I will not allow you to go back to sleep, and especially not a third time!

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.640
This time, you will not escape!

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.660
This is the moment you awaken...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.460
There will be no other time!

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.800
This time...

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.120
This time you will receive your special technique!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.330
We meet again, Sakata Gintoki.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.810
Or rather, my master!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.310
Y-You're...

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.230
Uh...

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.040
Excuse me, who are—No, wait!

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.820
I-It's great to see you again.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.070
Oh, crap. Who's this guy?

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.070
Who <i>is</i> he?!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.100
Huh? I thought you knew him, Gin.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.850
I was just humoring him... I totally don't remember.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.220
What about you?

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.640
I've never seen him before. Kagura?

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.920
Even if I knew that nasty looking
beardo, I'd pretend I didn't!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.710
Hey, stupid! Pipe down, he'll hear you!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.710
Maybe we'll remember after we hear his name?

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.090
No way, man. He fully expects that we remember him.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.630
He was trying to act super cool. That'd ruin the mood!

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.680
He'd be embarrassed! He'd turn bright red!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.740
I get the feeling he already is...

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.140
He's already turning red.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.010
Uh, I think he was Mr. Sawatari...

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:58.940
Uh, I'm pretty sure he's not a Sawatari.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.900
He seems kind of supernatural, actually.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.930
How spooky he is doesn't really matter if we can't remember his name.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.850
He's Sawatari, right?

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.280
Wait, who's Sawatari again?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:10.120
Oh, I think I know! Isn't he the Sawatari from Bleach?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.960
There's no one that lame looking in Bleach! And who's Sawatari anyway?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.520
Uh, he's been waiting for a while now. He's starting to really look frustrated.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.740
Oh crap! One of you has to remember!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.260
Who the hell is he? Where did we meet Sawatari in the first place?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.750
Cough cough...

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.340
Cough cough—the spirit—cough!

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.000
I think he's trying to disguise giving us a hint by coughing!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.070
Cough cough—around the end of year two—cough!

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.390
Huh? What was that about year two?

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.060
Cough cough! Could you repeat that? Cough cough cough.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.070
Cough cough—Around New Year of 2008—coughcoughcough!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.850
Year 2? The year 2000?

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.660
Cough cough! One more time please! Cough!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.510
Cough! Cough! I just said—cough!

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:53.530
Around the end of year two—cough cough—episode 89—cough!

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:57.670
That was me—cough cough—the spirit of Lake Touya! Cough cough!

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:02.920
Cough cough! Wait, you spit? You're 89 years old and spit? 200 years old? Cough cough cough!

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.840
No! Cough! The spirit!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.710
I'm the spirit of Lake Touya! Coughcoughcough!

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.010
Could you two please talk normally now?

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.720
Oh, yeah, the spirit!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.930
The spirit of Lake Touya that showed up at the end of year two!

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.280
Dammit, this is bad! Who's the
spirit of Lake Touya again?

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:19.870
No clue.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.020
You don't even remember what happened!

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:28.730
I am the spirit of Lake Touya, who showed up to teach you all a special technique around New Year's!

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.160
I get the vague feeling that may have happened...

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.540
I don't think so, though.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.530
Did I make no impression on you at all?!

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.360
I know this might sound pompous,
but I'm a pretty unique guy!

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.290
Sorry. I make it a point to forget about unpleasant experiences.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:44.420
Well... What does a spirit want with us, exactly?

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.820
That's obvious.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:49.310
This time, I will have you all learn your special technique.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:52.310
Last time you refused to learn it, of all things,

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.270
and all I was able to teach you was a simple attack (The Thigh Smack)...

00:06:56.270 --> 00:07:00.930
But now, you should understand the value of a special technique on a fundamental level!

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.940
What do you mean?

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.550
Because the anime ended!

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.610
What is this spirit talking about?!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.370
I warned you...

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.720
A special technique is crucially important!

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.250
It has nothing to do with wanting to get stronger,

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.440
it's an important part of doing business!

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.850
This spirit isn't holding back!

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.460
He's recommending special techniques on the grounds of business concerns!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.170
Listen well... I will once again teach you the true importance of a special technique.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.720
As you know, anime series are
a powerful form of advertising...

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.680
However, they require a large amount of money to be created!

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.700
And in order to get that money...

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.110
You need sponsors!

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.810
What does any of this have to do
with special techniques, spirit?!

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.900
Sponsors invest a large amount of money into the creation of an anime...

00:07:48.570 --> 00:08:01.330
Anime
We can make stuff sell,
so fork over the cash

00:07:48.570 --> 00:08:01.330
Sponsor
We'll fork over the cash,
so you make stuff sell

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.650
In exchange, the sponsors use the anime

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:55.010
in order to advertise their products, in a mutually beneficial fashion!

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:56.780
That is the nature of the agreement.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.480
Just getting down to the nitty gritty, aren't you?!

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.330
Besides, we don't need to know special techniques for making anime!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:07.310
The amount of merchandise made when an anime goes into production is determined by the sponsors!

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.840
In other words, if this merchandise does not sell...

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.350
It leaves the transaction incomplete, so the sponsors leave, meaning no more anime!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.200
Now, amid this crucial merchandising scheme,

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.260
do you know what often pays the most potent dividends?

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.230
None other than...

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.150
Video games!

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.730
What is wrong with this spirit?!
What is he even here for?!

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.160
We had a video game last year, though.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.490
It was... uh, let's see...

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.890
One of those Momotaro Dentetsu or
Itagaki Street style party games, I think.

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:38.160
Part of the problem is that the board game ended up the way it did in the first place!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.830
Hey, come on! The guys at Bamco tried their best!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.720
Games are sold at a high unit price, which naturally makes for big profits upon sale.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.430
And among the easiest to sell titles are...

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:49.000
Fighting Street Too

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.220
Fighting games.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:57.610
The easy accessibility of fighting games make for stable sales, a truly top-notch product!

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:59.070
I'm not sure I ever want to buy one again now.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.020
You're ruining the value of your top-notch product!

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:08.580
And of course, special moves are a
necessary element of fighting games.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.150
Do you understand?

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.920
You didn't simply refuse the chance to get a fighting game made on that day,

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.580
you shortened your very own future!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:22.330
A special technique isn't something
you hit an enemy with...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.420
It's something you use on sponsors!

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.040
This guy pretty clearly isn't a spirit, right? He's from the marketing branch of some company, right?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.400
It is not too late!

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.290
You must learn a special technique to draw in sponsors!

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:37.380
If the anime comes up with it, it can then go on to appear in the original manga!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.380
You've seen countless examples of such a thing!

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:44.430
Once the anime ends, the manga <i>feels</i>
basically over and it loses all its vitality!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.320
Stop trying to freak us out!

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.760
If the original manga ends, then the anime has no chance of being revived!

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.320
Okay, we need to shut him up, or he could really say something problematic.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.660
There's no way we can learn a special technique after all this time.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.780
Our show is over! What sense does that make?

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:05.080
Even if we learn it, you can't make a game unless everyone else has one, too!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.580
That matter's already taken care of.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.550
I have people in place.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:11.300
A monitor?

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:14.090
Please respond. This is the spirit of Lake Touya!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:19.340
Crotch

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.180
Yes. This is the spirit of Matamune speaking.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:18.970
It's a different spirit!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.470
How are things going?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.100
Eh, okay I guess.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.860
He's got a knack for this...

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.350
I think he'll have it mastered shortly.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.350
Katsura?!

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.150
What's going on here?!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.880
Okay, focus, and try again!

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:36.960
That is the spirit of that man's sword, the Matamune,

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.890
Right!

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.510
the spirit of Matamune.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:42.350
Spirits are now teaching assorted
characters their special techniques.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.910
You guys are doing this stupid crap all over the place?!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.910
If you people continue to hesitate,

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:52.500
you will be left behind by the others, as they master their techniques, and grow stronger!

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:56.800
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong! Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.130
What the hell kind of training is this?!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:11.970
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:02.580
It's a special technique to get a sponsorship from a cell phone provider.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.140
What kind of technique is that?! You just want to get him in a commercial!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.630
And that's old! How many years ago
did that one air, anyway?!

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.220
Again!

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:12.820
Do you think you can compete with Kaela with such paltry cuteness?!

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:12.820
Right!

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.820
There's no way he can beat her!

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.020
No one wants a nasty looking
cell phone like you anyway!

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.280
And this <i>is</i> old!

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:19.280
Ring—

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:24.580
What about the fighting game?
How can he use that one in a game?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.710
This is just one example.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:28.790
There are other spirits at work...

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.130
Please respond. This is the spirit of Lake Touya.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.210
Sunglasses spirit, please respond.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.470
Sunglasses spirit?!

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.340
Even sunglasses have spirits in them?!

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.130
Yes, this is the Sunglasses spirit.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.340
This is the same lady from before!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.310
You just have her working with multiple people!

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.850
She just crossed out the old mark on her forehead!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.740
You're wrong! That's my mo—I mean, the Sunglasses spirit.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.110
You almost said mom! That's your mom?!

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.850
How are things going, sunglasses spirit?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.360
I'm having him work on it right now.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.330
He was able to split up pretty well...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.570
Hey! Why would you teach a fancy move like that to the least important dude in the cast?!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.460
Your dear mom forgot what was supposed to come next, though.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:05.320
Err, the Sunglasses spirit.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:06.890
You don't have to hide it anymore.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.920
Ringo-dan-dan-chin-gong-dong-dong!

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.730
Was it ringo-dan-chin or ringo-dong-chin?

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.380
They're pretending to be Kaela too?!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.280
I'm sorry, but I'm not very familiar with Kaela...

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:20.870
I see. Well, I'll have to teach him something else, then.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.680
Why?!

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:25.800
Creating copies of yourself is already a great special technique! Why bring Kaela into it at all?!

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.380
What is wrong with these spirits?! Why are you trying to compete with Kaela?!

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.440
Uh, this is the spirit of Lake Touya...

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.120
Cabaret Club spirit, please respond.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.270
Cabaret Club spirit?! That just sounds like a regular old guy! You're just like a TV producer!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.010
Hi! Daddy's here!

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:41.930
He spilled the beans. First thing he did was lay it bare.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:45.100
Not Dad! You're the Cabaret Club spirit! Get it right!

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.800
Oh, right! My bad, my bad.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.670
I'm the Cabaret Club spirit~!

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.540
You people are just doing some weird family activity!

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:55.920
I'm teaching this hostess her special technique as we speak, ring-a-ding-dong.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.290
Why are they treating say that like saying "over" on the radio now?!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.360
How is it going, ring-a-ding-ding-dong?

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.760
Everything looks good so far, ring-a-ding-dong.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.300
You people just want to say ring-a-ding-dong!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:10.310
The only thing is, she caught on faster than I anticipated...

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:12.910
Sister?!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.850
Ring...

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.610
Ding-ding-Dodonpa!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.030
She's about as strong as Lord Frieza right now... Is that gonna be a problem?

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.080
Now the balance of strength is all out of whack!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.440
Dammit, honey!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.460
Why are you at a cabaret club again?!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:36.930
His mom just jumped into the conversation...

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:38.800
Would you give it a rest?!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.900
You're a father! Aren't you embarrassed?!

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.750
Calm down Mo—er, Sunglasses spirit!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.010
And he's not my father, he's the Cabaret Club spirit!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:48.000
W-What am I supposed to do?! It's part of my job!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.260
A mother shouldn't gripe about this stuff in front of the boy!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.940
She's not my mother! She's the Sunglasses spirit!

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:54.600
This has completely gone out of control.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.730
I know you were talking about "teaching an even better special technique"

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.860
and getting mixed up with one of those hostesses!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.070
I know what you're up to!

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.990
What?! I know you were with that pipe guy from the water company the other day

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:10.910
using special moves and getting them used on you a whole bunch!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.370
What are we talking about here?!

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.780
I can't believe you! You're doubting me?!

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.600
I have absolutely had it with you!

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.780
I'm moving back in with my parents!

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.840
Hey, hey, come on, ma'am, calm down...

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.220
It was just a figure of speech.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:23.840
That's right!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.170
He's using his special technique to break up the argument!

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.240
Yeah, why don't you just run off?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.040
Maybe you can have someone else check
out your pipes or whatever else you want!

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.720
Come on, sir, that's going too far.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.170
Shut it! What the hell do you know?!

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.700
Come on, easy does it...

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.120
Shut up!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.080
I told your ass to calm down.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.570
You deaf or something?

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.960
Caba... Daaaaad!

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:59.330
There it is! He finally admitted it!

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.130
Please respond!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:05.110
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong! Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.850
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding—

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:13.300
T-The signal from Cabaret Club spirit's ring-a-ding-dong is dead...

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.800
This is impossible!

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:19.210
Has she learned enough special
techniques to defeat a spirit?!

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:26.030
We may have given birth to an unstoppable monster...

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.620
Please respond... Please respond...

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.610
What...?

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.570
Spirit of Lake Touya... Please respond...

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.610
Mom!

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:40.330
I'm not your mom anymore...

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.580
I'm just a divorced spirit, now...

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:47.090
Well, I was thinking about it,
but it doesn't look like I can.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:51.590
This failure of a spirit... I can't leave him alone.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:57.490
It looks like the two of us are
the spirits of a foolish marriage...

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.600
M-Mother...

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.800
Hey, what are they doing? Why's it so dramatic all of a sudden?

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:06.850
Mom!

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.440
Tou...

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:14.110
If that monster gets back to the Earth, it'll mean the end of the world.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:17.890
Hey, could you please stop calling my sister a monster?

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.990
You're the only one who can stop her.

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:21.910
This is your fault in the first place.

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:25.630
A spirit's duty is to hand down special techniques...

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.420
You must teach them!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:32.330
Teach them an amazing special technique that can stop that monster...

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:38.050
I'm sure my students will do what they can to help.

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.060
How the hell's that gonna help?!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:42.810
M-Mom! She's—

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:48.690
Mom! Dad!

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:50.790
Tou...

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:55.730
Ring..a...ding...dong...

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:09.210
Ring-a-ding-ding... dong.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.920
All of you, listen to me!

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.200
The time to awaken has come!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:20.970
Now I will teach you the ultimate technique!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:27.850
With this, I know you'll be guaranteed to get a lot of sponsors!

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:32.650
She's here!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.450
Here it goes! Watch closely!

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:41.160
This is the ultimate technique!

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:47.190
I'm really sorry!

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.680
Let this sight be burnt into your eyes.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.410
This is the ultimate technique...

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:58.760
The Dogeza.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:03.460
Don't want it!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.440
Ring-a-ding-dong, ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:11.730
Classic Commercial Special

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:24.640
Ring-a-ding-dong, ring-a-ding-ding-

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.640
Stop!

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.120
Hang on a sec! Hold it!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.080
What is this? It's over?!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.250
That little bit right there is all?!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.720
That's right. Good work everybody.

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:33.360
Good work.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.470
Yeah, good work!

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.050
What?! No, no this can't be right!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.200
I heard we were coming back temporarily...

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.640
So I thought for sure we'd get to show up...

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.740
I even learned a special technique to turn into a gorilla!

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.480
You were plenty gorilla before you learned to transform!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.250
Kondo...

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.920
Don't worry about it.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:54.240
You don't need to sweat turning into a gorilla just to make an appearance.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.900
You say that...

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:59.840
But it looks like you learned how to make duplicates of mayonnaise, Hijikata...

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.510
Seems to me you were pretty excited, too.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.840
No! Stupid!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.990
I just bought these because they were on sale over at the supermarket!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.700
While we're on the subject...

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:11.800
I learned how to take naps without wearing an eye mask...

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:14.500
You already nap all the damn time without a special technique!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.120
Why are we doing an episode
about special moves, anyway?!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:20.780
If we're gonna do a one-shot it should be "The Record of Shinsengumi Bloodshed!"

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.610
You still haven't given up on that yet?

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:25.150
That promo was just to trick
people into watching, dumbass!

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.130
What'd you say?!

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.020
That's right!

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:33.150
Y-Yamazaki? Why are you dressed like that...?

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.900
Nobody cares about our record of bloodshed...

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.240
What we should have done was...

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:41.740
Monja!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.640
Wait, why monja?! What happened to anpan?!

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:48.090
W-What is this? Monjayaki batter?

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:50.110
It is, right? It's not something else, is it?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.870
I think so... but stay away, just in case.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:55.070
Somebody give me something to wipe this off with!

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.970
Don't look this way—

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.470
Hey, you're barfing!

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.220
This stuff is just monja, right?! Right?!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.260
I've got more...

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.340
Oh, crap!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.750
Mon—

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.370
S-Sacchan?!

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.780
You all don't understand anything.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:13.390
The key visual poster made it obvious enough to me...

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.190
What we should have made this about was—

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:20.400
An exciting live 8-hour marathon featuring Gin and me!

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:23.030
What are you, some kind of celebrity from the economic bubble?! No way we'd do that!

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.720
Gin! Take me like it's our wedding night!

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:30.100
Great, now you're barfing too!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.160
This really <i>is</i> just monja, right?!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.560
That's right! Me too...

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.850
We could broadcast my quiet,
peaceful married life with Otae

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:40.010
in a an excruciatingly detailed documentary covering every single butt hair! We can't let this e—

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:45.250
Hello? I think I've found a gorilla that escaped from the zoo.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:46.620
I'm requesting permission to kill it.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.720
I'm pretty sure you tried to kill him before you called it in!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.700
By the way, how long until a story starring me where I grow to an F-Cup,

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.740
"The Mega-Tits Uproar Association"?

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:58.350
Uh, I'm sorry but I'm pretty sure no story like that is even in the planning stages...

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.090
We don't have much time left, right?

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:04.000
We can't let this end without doing a Mega-Tits story!

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:07.070
What about the dojo's restoration?!
Shouldn't you be worried about that?!

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:12.360
I never got to throw my sukonbu and egg rice dish tasting party either... What should we do?

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:13.750
Do it on your own time!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:18.130
Sadaharu is worried about what was going on with all that Inugami stuff, too.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.340
Quit digging that stuff up! I know you're a dog, but quit digging!

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.220
Hold it right there...

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:26.770
We've got some unfinished business, too.

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:27.970
Granny?!

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:28.390
Rent

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:31.040
You need to pay back your rent and...

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:35.100
Until I get to Agerunrun into Haggyness Charge TamaCure, we can't let it end!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.850
No TamaCure!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.800
Come on, let's not sweat the small stuff this time...

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:41.380
Since this is a limited renewal,
we can just write it off, y'know?

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.290
Not happening!

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.160
Hey! Hold it!

00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:49.450
Mail's here.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:52.450
What is this?!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.730
Will Ryoma show up on next year's NHK Taiga theater?

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:57.290
How should I know?!

00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:00.290
Gin! Are we not getting any more screen time either?

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:03.300
Don't be stupid. We still haven't
done Real Life Real Heart yet.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:00.750
Don't Forget To
Keep Watching

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:06.320
Hey, Gin! You have to take control, here!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:09.300
Shut up!

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:12.880
Quit your stupid yelping already.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:15.260
You fools just start puberty or something?

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:20.310
It all started with that line, didn't it?

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:23.070
Gin...

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:26.180
Makes you think about how far we've come, doesn't it?

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:30.320
A lot happened, but it feels like it flew by.

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:36.620
But y'know, some things are better off ending before they're quite finished, don't you think?

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:40.940
A party is fun because you're sad when it's over.

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.280
We've already ended.

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:48.080
And we made an incredible exit, while we were at it.

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:52.430
It's better this way.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:01.440
Plus, now we don't have to worry about wrapping up my backstory or my time as the White Devil!

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:08.190
You're just being lazy?!

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:11.870
The End

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:18.960
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:40.340
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong-ding-dong!

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:47.890
Why's your weather so dreary?

00:23:47.890 --> 00:23:53.470
Can't you see how clear my sky is?

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:58.790
You can borrow my favorite umbrella.

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:05.580
So that you might stop crying.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:08.320
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:16.660
Let's all share it together.

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:19.280
Ring-a-ding-dong ring-a-ding-ding-dong!

00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:27.900
Do-re-mi-fa-mi-re-do!

00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.360
Ring-a-ding-dong!
